d38c","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":13,"p":[20,20],"r":[23,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"This is a quotation from the LX.. of Jer. xxiii. 18, where for u 9posth/mati Aqula has ἀπορρήτω and Symmachus o 9mili/a , (according to Trommius). u 9po/sthma properly means a Station of troops, and such is the meaning in the other two places where the word occurs in the LXX., viz.: - 2Sam. xxiii. 14, and 1 Chron. xi. 16. The Hebrew word which it represents in this passage is one of frequent use, and means \"a Council,\" or, in a sense derived from this, Familiar Intercourse. In Job xv. 8 it is rendered in A.V. The Secret of God, where the LXX.. has σύνταγυα . The Vulgate in both cases has Concilium Dei; the Benedictines however render it Substance. A.V.. has Counsel, and in marg. Secret; while R.V. reads Council, with no marginal alternative."},{"id":"3b06efc26ac9","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":20,"p":[22,22],"r":[6,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Sam. vi. 14."},{"id":"d71ac3a6d3d6","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":25,"p":[56,56],"r":[12,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Sam. xii. 16."},{"id":"1f1723057097","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":25,"p":[75,75],"r":[5,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Sam. v. 1."},{"id":"29fbc7b3828f","v":"npnf.ephraem.hymni_de_nativitate","w":"ephraem.hymni_de_nativitate","a":"ephram_der_syrer","s":9,"p":[8,8],"r":[6,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Sam. vi. 23."},{"id":"1a35773c42da","v":"npnf.cassian.de_institutis","w":"cassian.de_institutis","a":"johannes_cassian","s":8,"p":[26,26],"r":[23,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Sam. xxiii. 17."},{"id